  × This request has a body, but its method is GET.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ fetch(url, { method: "GET", body: "x" } as RequestInit);
      │                             ^^^^
    3 │ fetch(url, { method: "GET", body: "x" } satisfies RequestInit);
    4 │ fetch(url, { method: "GET", body: "x" }!);
  
  i Requests that use the GET or HEAD method can't have a body, so this code throws a TypeError when it runs. A request without a method uses GET.
  
  i Remove the body, or use a method that allows one, such as POST.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

